import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy | TassieNow" description="Privacy practices for TassieNow visitors and people submitting enquiries.">
 <section class="content-page">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>TassieNow is an independent Tasmanian discovery service. You can browse places and events without creating an account.</p>
  <h2>Information we handle</h2>
  <p>When you choose Near Me, your browser requests location permission. The location is used in your browser to calculate nearby listings; TassieNow does not require you to submit precise coordinates to use the directory.</p>
  <p>When you submit a form, we may process the name, contact details, listing information and message you provide to respond, review corrections or manage your enquiry. Do not include sensitive information that is not necessary for your request.</p>
  <h2>Accounts, saved places and plans</h2>
  <p>Creating an account stores your email address, display name, password hash and hashed recovery code in Cloudflare D1. Your email is private and is not verified by an email confirmation service. An essential, secure, HttpOnly session cookie keeps you logged in for up to 30 days. Saved places, dated plans and plan notes are private to your account. Cloudflare Turnstile checks account access and contributions to help prevent abuse; short-lived hashed rate-limit keys help protect the service.</p>
  <h2>Reviews and photographs</h2>
  <p>Your display name is shown with approved reviews and photos. Submissions may be reviewed by an automated moderation assistant. Pending contribution text and photos are temporarily copied to a private review workspace for up to one day; signup names and emails are excluded from these review copies. Approval updates and rejection reasons are delivered through private account messages. Submissions are held for moderation before publication; pending submissions are visible to you and the owner. Only upload photos you own and have permission to share. Photos are resized in your browser and image metadata, including embedded GPS information, is stripped before storage. Avoid sensitive information in captions, reviews or photos.</p>
  <p>You can delete contributions or permanently delete your account through My TassieNow. Account deletion removes saved places, plans, reviews, uploaded photos and active sessions from the live service. Cloudflare recovery backups and operational security logs may retain records temporarily under the hosting provider's retention policies.</p>
  <h2>Analytics and technical logs</h2>
  <p>To improve discovery and show aggregate referral activity, TassieNow may count first-party page views, filter/search interactions and categories of outbound clicks by page and day. These counters do not store your search words, precise location, IP address or an identifying visitor ID. A browser Do Not Track or Global Privacy Control signal disables the first-party counters. These are interaction counts, not unique visitors.</p>
  <p>TassieNow may use Cloudflare's privacy-conscious web analytics and essential server security logs to understand use, diagnose faults and prevent abuse. External booking, map and business websites have their own privacy practices.</p>
  <p>Some photographs use rights-verified external image URLs and load directly from the original media host. Viewing such pages may send a request to that third-party host. TassieNow shows attribution, licence and original source alongside the photograph.</p>
 <h2>Advertising and affiliate partners</h2>
  <p>TassieNow displays clearly labelled affiliate links to third-party partners, including PlayAsia, ElevenLabs and Meshy. Following these links takes you to their websites, which may use their own cookies or referral tracking. TassieNow may receive a commission if you make a qualifying purchase, at no extra cost to you.</p>
  <p>TassieNow uses Google AdSense to display advertisements. Google and its partners may use cookies and similar technologies to deliver and measure ads, subject to applicable privacy and consent settings. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google advertising privacy information</a>.</p>
  <h2>Corrections and privacy enquiries</h2>
  <p>To request a correction or ask about personal information in a submission, use the contact or enquiry channels linked on this website. We review requests before changing published records.</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>This notice may be updated as the site's features and commercial arrangements develop. Last updated: 16 October 2026.</p>
 </section>
</BaseLayout>